{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1523532-bloodlines-the-resurrected-revised-coming-soon","id":1523532,"title":"Bloodlines: The Resurrected REVISED coming soon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-03T22:46:16-07:00","id":1523532,"title":"Bloodlines: The Resurrected REVISED coming soon","content":"Edit: It's here!<br /> <br /> Book alone: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/456171/Bloodlines-The-Resurrected?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...iate_id=321925</a><br /> Previous Purchaser Discount bundle: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/456174/Resurrected-Discount-Bundle-BUNDLE?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/p...ed-Discount-Bundle-BUNDLE?affiliate_id=321925</a><br /> If you haven't got <b>Requiem for Rome Second Edition</b>, this is the lowest price you can get it, and we're including the early-bird price on <b>Resurrected 2.0</b>: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/456192/Resurrected-in-Rome-BUNDLE?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...iate_id=321925</a>\u200b<br /> <br /> <i><b>The prices on both these are MARKED DOWN TODAY ONLY (October 11). The bundle will still be there tomorrow, but both will be going slightly up in price at noon tomorrow, so if you wanna get it cheap, get it now!\u200b</b></i><br /> <br /> TL;DR: NMD is putting out a <i>massive </i>new version of <b>Bloodlines: The Resurrected </b>next week: noon PST on Wednesday the 11th. If you already have the old version, you'll be able to get it for cheap.<br /> <br /> Hello again! It's been a while! I just wanted to drop in to let you know None More Dark Publishing's latest project is coming out next week: <b>Bloodlines: The Resurrected \u2014 Revised</b>. If you know anything about us, you probably recognize that title. That was the first book we ever put out, as a kind of short mechanical patch for a bunch of vampire bloodlines from the old Hidden, Chosen, and Legendary books. I laid it out in Microsoft Word and got art from a stock site that I\u2019m pretty sure doesn\u2019t exist anymore.<br /> <br /> Despite being a bit rough regarding production values, it did pretty well! I think it\u2019s at about ~520 sales at this point, which is a lot in terms of community content. But, it\u2019s always been the odd man out in our work. There\u2019s no lore or context for any of the bloodlines in the book, just page references to no less than seven older books if you want to know more.<br /> <br /> This has always bothered me, more so as we did our clan book series and started to treat these books in a more professional way instead of kind of a lark. To get to the point, <b>Bloodlines: The Resurrected \u2014 Revised </b>is the book I\u2019ve wanted to put out pretty much since we released the first version. <b>Assuming no disasters, it's coming out on the 11th this month, 12:00 PST</b>. It includes full backstories for its bloodlines, brand-new mechanics for each lineage on top of what was in the previous version, and full illustrations. We\u2019ve also added two additional bloodline updates, in the form of the infamous Players and the storytelling Taifa.<br /> <br /> This also includes a massive expansion of the Necromancy system we included in the original, as well as the Harbingers from <b>The Danse Macabre</b>, who I\u2019ve wanted to update for <i>years</i>. Furthermore, you\u2019ll find a hugely beefed-up version of the original\u2019s quick conversion appendix, with 28 quick-bite bloodlines you can plug into your chronicle without a lot of fuss. We\u2019re also ALSO including errata for some bloodline systems for a few previous releases, including a rework of Crochan from <b>Dark Eras 2</b> to bring it more in line with the Requiem Discipline design aesthetic.<br /> <br /> What I\u2019m trying to say is, that even if you have the original (which I believe is about 27 pages or so), you\u2019re going to want this. This one clocks in at 90 pages, more than triple the old one. I know that can be a hard sell, especially because I\u2019m pretty sure everyone and their dog has this one, so we\u2019re going to be offering this in a bundle with the old version so you can get it for cheap if you bought it before. We\u2019ll also have bundles with <b>Requiem for Rome</b> and other books if you haven\u2019t checked them out yet. I also know a LOT of people really want us to do something like this for <b>Bloodlines: The Devoted</b>, and I can promise that, if this does well, that'll be moved up on the docket.<br /> <br /> I'll be previewing things over at the RPG.net forums, but feel free to ask any questions you might have here as well:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/vampire-bloodlines-the-resurrected-revised-previews-q-a.914044/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...ws-q-a.914044/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 10-11-2023, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T05:27:12-07:00","id":1523541,"title":"","content":"Sweet! Looking forward to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1494-deranged-goblin","name":"Deranged Goblin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T08:20:29-07:00","id":1523550,"title":"","content":"Hell ya! I'm excited for this. I noticed the original necromancy didn't actually do a whole lot with ghosts, can you tell us if the new one deals with them more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T08:44:56-07:00","id":1523552,"title":"","content":"That's wonderful news!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T13:36:16-07:00","id":1523571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1523532-bloodlines-the-resurrected-revised-coming-soon?p=1523550#post1523550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell ya! I'm excited for this. I noticed the original necromancy didn't actually do a whole lot with ghosts, can you tell us if the new one deals with them more?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there are definitely a few more ghostly rites! Part of the reason the original is so zombie-heavy is because a lot of the 1E bloodlines we converted were <i>also </i>very corpse-oriented, and many of the rites were based on those. For some reason, a lot of 1E necromantic powers avoided ghosts (we were talking about this the other day, funny enough). Anyway, you'll have lots to go on for wraiths. I believe the original had about 19 rites in total, whereas this one has 39 or so, not even including covenant/bloodline-exclusive ones.<br /> <br /> Also, anyone interested in checking out the Harbingers, I just previewed them in the link above!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T14:47:02-07:00","id":1523574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1523532-bloodlines-the-resurrected-revised-coming-soon?p=1523571#post1523571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, there are definitely a few more ghostly rites! Part of the reason the original is so zombie-heavy is because a lot of the 1E bloodlines we converted were <i>also </i>very corpse-oriented, and many of the rites were based on those. For some reason, a lot of 1E necromantic powers avoided ghosts (we were talking about this the other day, funny enough). Anyway, you'll have lots to go on for wraiths. I believe the original had about 19 rites in total, whereas this one has 39 or so, not even including covenant/bloodline-exclusive ones.<br /> <br /> Also, anyone interested in checking out the Harbingers, I just previewed them in the link above!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's awesome to hear! My Requiem for Rome Apollonaire is very much looking forward to it. I was always a bit disappointed that necromancy didn't get any new rituals in <i>Desecrated Rites</i> so this is going to fill that gap nicely!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T10:59:10-07:00","id":1523645,"title":"","content":"one problem I had with ressurected was Gaalloi dont depend on blood baths to be beautiful anymore","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"